<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="2PE" style="id">2 PETER</book>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2PE 1"/>
  <para style="s1">Greeting</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2PE 1:1"/>
    Simeon Peter, one who belongs entirely to Jesus Christ as His servant, and is sent with apostolic authority,
    <verse eid="2PE 1:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">To those who have received a faith equally precious as ours through the righteousness of our God and Savior Jesus Christ:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2PE 1:2"/>
    May grace and peace be abundantly increased to you through the knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2PE 1:3"/>
    His divine power has granted to us all things necessary for living and for godliness through the knowledge of the One who summoned us to His own glory and virtue,
    <verse eid="2PE 1:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2PE 1:4"/>
    through which He has bestowed on us His precious and magnificent promises, so that through these you might become sharers in God’s nature, having fled from the spiritual and moral decay that is in the world through sinful craving.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Spiritual Qualities in Increasing Measure</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2PE 1:5"/>
    For this precise reason, apply all diligence to add to your faith moral excellence, and to moral excellence add knowledge,
    <verse eid="2PE 1:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2PE 1:6"/>
    and to knowledge add self-discipline, and to self-discipline add patient endurance, and to patient endurance add godliness,
    <verse eid="2PE 1:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2PE 1:7"/>
    and to godliness add brotherly kindness, and to brotherly kindness add love.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2PE 1:8"/>
    For if these qualities belong to you and are increasing, they keep you from being useless or barren in the knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2PE 1:9"/>
    For whoever lacks these qualities is spiritually shortsighted to the point of blindness, having become forgetful of the cleansing he received from his former sins.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2PE 1:10"/>
    Therefore, brothers and sisters, be even more zealous to make certain your calling and election, for if you practice these things, you will absolutely never stumble.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2PE 1:11"/>
    For in this manner, entry into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ will be abundantly supplied to you.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Peter’s Imminent Death</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2PE 1:12"/>
    Therefore, I intend to keep reminding you concerning these matters, even though you already know them and stand firm in the truth that is present with you.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2PE 1:13"/>
    I regard it as right, as long as I remain in this bodily tent, to awaken you by means of reminder,
    <verse eid="2PE 1:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2PE 1:14"/>
    knowing that the putting off of my bodily tent is coming soon, just as our Lord Jesus Christ revealed to me.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2PE 1:15"/>
    And I will endeavor to ensure that after my departure you will always have the ability to remember these things.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Christ’s Honor and Glory, and the Prophetic Word</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2PE 1:16"/>
    For we did not follow artfully fabricated myths when we made known to you the power and appearing of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we had become eyewitnesses of His magnificence.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2PE 1:17"/>
    For He received honor and glory from God the Father when a voice came to Him from the magnificent glory, declaring, “This is My Son, My Beloved One, in whom My delight rests”*—
    <verse eid="2PE 1:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2PE 1:18"/>
    and we ourselves heard this voice borne from heaven when we were with Him on the holy mountain.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2PE 1:19"/>
    And we possess the prophetic word made more reliable, to which you do well to pay careful attention, as to a lamp giving light in a murky place, until the day breaks and the morning star arises in your hearts.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2PE 1:20"/>
    Understanding this first of all, that no prophecy of Scripture originates from one’s private interpretation.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2PE 1:21"/>
    For prophecy never came by human initiative, but people spoke from God as they were borne along by the Holy Spirit.
    <verse eid="2PE 1:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">17 See Matt. 17:5; Mk. 9:7; Lk. 9:35</para>
  <chapter eid="2PE 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="2PE 2"/>
  <para style="s1">The Condemnation of the False Prophets and False Teachers</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2PE 2:1"/>
    But false prophets also appeared among the people, just as there will also be false teachers among you, who will surreptitiously introduce destructive heresies, even repudiating the Master who bought them, bringing upon themselves swift destruction.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2PE 2:2"/>
    And many will follow their licentious practices, and because of them the way of truth will be blasphemed.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2PE 2:3"/>
    And driven by greed, they will exploit you with fabricated arguments. The judgment pronounced against them long ago has not been suspended, and their destruction is not delayed.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2PE 2:4"/>
    For God did not withhold judgment from angels who rebelled. Instead, He cast them down into Tartarus, consigning them to utter darkness where they are kept under restraint, awaiting final judgment.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2PE 2:5"/>
    Nor did He hold back judgment from the ancient world. When He brought the flood upon a society that had rejected Him, He preserved Noah—a preacher of righteousness—together with seven others.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2PE 2:6"/>
    Likewise, He condemned Sodom and Gomorrah, reducing those cities to ruin and turning them into a lasting warning of what awaits those who persist in godlessness.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2PE 2:7"/>
    Yet at the same time, He rescued righteous Lot, who was deeply distressed by the unrestrained and immoral behavior of lawless people around him.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2PE 2:8"/>
    Living among them day after day, that righteous man was inwardly tormented as he witnessed and heard their continual acts of defiance against God.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2PE 2:9"/>
    From all this we learn that the Lord knows how to deliver the godly from trial, while at the same time keeping the unrighteous under punishment until the day when judgment is finally executed.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2PE 2:10"/>
    This judgment falls especially on those who surrender themselves to corrupt bodily desires and who treat all authority with contempt.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">They are reckless, arrogant, and self-assertive, and they show no fear when they speak abusively against the glorious ones. </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2PE 2:11"/>
    Even angels—who surpass them in strength and power—do not bring slanderous accusations against them in the presence of the Lord.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2PE 2:12"/>
    Yet these individuals resemble irrational beasts—creatures governed solely by instinct, bred for capture and slaughter. They pronounce judgment upon matters of which they possess no understanding, and in the very destruction that befalls such animals, they too shall perish.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2PE 2:13"/>
    Their suffering will be the fitting return for the harm they cause. They take pleasure in shameless self-indulgence even in public. They are moral stains within the community, openly delighting in their deceptive excesses while sharing meals among you.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2PE 2:14"/>
    Their gaze is saturated with lust for an adultress, and they are incapable of breaking free from sin. They prey on those whose faith is unstable. Their hearts have been disciplined—not in godliness, but in greed. Accursed children! 
    <verse eid="2PE 2:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2PE 2:15"/>
    By leaving the straight path, they have gone astray, choosing to follow the example of Balaam son of Beor, who was drawn by the reward of unrighteous gain.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2PE 2:16"/>
    Yet Balaam was exposed for his own lawlessness when a mute animal spoke with a human voice and restrained the prophet’s reckless madness.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2PE 2:17"/>
    These people offer nothing of substance—like springs with no water or clouds driven aimlessly by violent winds. What has been kept for them is the deepest darkness.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2PE 2:18"/>
    With inflated and empty speech, they entice people through sensual desires of the flesh—those who are only just breaking free from those who live in deception.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:18"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" sid="2PE 2:19"/>
    They hold out the promise of freedom, yet they themselves are trapped in decay and moral slavery, since a person becomes enslaved to whatever gains mastery over them.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:19"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" sid="2PE 2:20"/>
    For if people escape the corruption of the world by coming to know the Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, and then become entangled again and overpowered by it, their condition at the end is worse than it was at the beginning.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:20"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" sid="2PE 2:21"/>
    It would have been better for them never to have come to know the path of righteousness than, after knowing it, to turn away from the holy commandment entrusted to them.
    <verse eid="2PE 2:21"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" sid="2PE 2:22"/>
    What has happened to them fits the old proverb perfectly: “A dog goes back to its vomit,” and “A pig that has been washed returns to wallowing in filth.*
    <verse eid="2PE 2:22"/>
  </para>
  <para style="s1">Notes</para>
  <para style="p">22 Quoted from Prov. 26:11</para>
  <chapter eid="2PE 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="2PE 3"/>
  <para style="s1">The Eschatological Day of the Lord</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2PE 3:1"/>
    Beloved, this is now the second time I have written to you. In both letters my aim has been to awaken your pure mind by calling certain truths back to your mind.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" sid="2PE 3:2"/>
    I want you to keep in view what was spoken earlier by the holy prophets, as well as the authoritative instruction of the Lord and Savior that came to you through your apostles.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:2"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" sid="2PE 3:3"/>
    Above all, you must recognize that as history moves toward its final stage, people will appear who scoff openly, advancing according to their own inordinate desires,
    <verse eid="2PE 3:3"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2PE 3:4"/>
    and who say, “So where is this promised return of Christ? Ever since our ancestors died, everything has gone on exactly the same way it has since the world first began.”
    <verse eid="2PE 3:4"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" sid="2PE 3:5"/>
    What they deliberately overlook is this: Long ago the heavens came into being, and the earth was shaped by the word of God out of water and through water,
    <verse eid="2PE 3:5"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" sid="2PE 3:6"/>
    and by those same waters the world that then existed was overwhelmed and destroyed.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:6"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2PE 3:7"/>
    By that very same divine word, the present heavens and earth are now being held in reserve, stored up not for water but for fire, awaiting the day when God judges and brings final ruin upon the ungodly.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:7"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" sid="2PE 3:8"/>
    But do not miss this crucial point, beloved: God’s experience of time is not like ours. What seems to us like a single day may be as long as a thousand years to Him, and a thousand years no more than a day.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:8"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2PE 3:9"/>
    The Lord is not failing to keep His promise, as some imagine when they accuse Him of delay. Rather, He is showing patience toward you, because He does not want anyone to be destroyed, but wants all to turn back to Him in repentance.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:9"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" sid="2PE 3:10"/>
    Nevertheless, the day of the Lord will arrive unexpectedly, like a thief. When it comes, the heavens will disappear with a deafening roar, the components of the universe will be destroyed by intense heat, and the earth together with everything done on it will be laid bare.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:10"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" sid="2PE 3:11"/>
    Since all of creation is going to be destroyed in this way, consider what kind of lives you ought to live—lives marked by holiness and godliness,
    <verse eid="2PE 3:11"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2PE 3:12"/>
    as you look forward to the day of God and even live in a way that hastens its arrival. Because of that day, the heavens will be set ablaze and dissolved, and the elements will melt away in burning heat.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:12"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" sid="2PE 3:13"/>
    Yet in keeping with the promise of God, we are waiting with confidence for new heavens and a new earth—where righteousness is fully at home.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:13"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" sid="2PE 3:14"/>
    For this reason, beloved, as you await these things, make every effort to be found by Him spotless, unblemished, and at peace.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:14"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" sid="2PE 3:15"/>
    You should understand the patience of our Lord as part of His saving purpose, just as our beloved brother Paul also wrote to you, according to the wisdom God gave him.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:15"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" sid="2PE 3:16"/>
    He speaks about these matters throughout his letters. Some of what he says is difficult to grasp, and people who are ignorant and spiritually unstable twist his words—just as they do the rest of Scripture—to their own ruin.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:16"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" sid="2PE 3:17"/>
    Since you already know these things, beloved, be on your guard so that you are not swept along by the deception of lawless people and lose your firm footing.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:17"/>
  </para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" sid="2PE 3:18"/>
    Instead, continue to grow—grow in the grace that comes from Christ and in the true knowledge of our Lord and Savior, Jesus Christ. To Him belongs the glory now and into the endless future. Amen.
    <verse eid="2PE 3:18"/>
  </para>
  <chapter eid="2PE 3"/>
</usx>
